// Over-rejection guard for hunt2 [06,07]: a closure passed to an applying-egressing param must still
// compile when its body captures nothing secret/tainted (returns a constant). Also guards the Part-1
// precision: a callee that does NOT egress the applied result never marks the param, so no false
// reject even for a secret-capturing closure — but here the capture is a constant, doubly safe.
fn run(cb) uses(net.send) { send("host", 80, cb(0)); }
fn main() uses(net.send) { run(|x| 42); }
